Package: SuperCell
Type: Package
Title: Simplification of Single-cell Data by Merging Together Highly Similar Cells
Version: 2.1.0
Authors@R: c(person("Léonard","Hérault",role=c("aut","cre"),email = "leonard.herault@gustaveroussy.fr"),person("Mariia","Bilous",role=c("aut"),email = "mariia.bilous@unil.ch"),person("Aurelie","Gabriel",role=c("aut"),email = "aurelie.gabriel@unil.ch"),person("David","Gfeller",role=c("aut"),email = "david.gfeller@unil.ch"),person("Matei","Teleman",role=c("ctb"),email = "matei.teleman@unil.ch"))
Description: Aggregates large single-cell and multimodal datasets into metacell datasets. The canonical grouped builder creates one native multimodal WNN graph per graph group, pools all conditions during graph construction, and splits memberships by condition only after clustering. Optional minimum-size repair uses affinity from that exact original shared WNN, is restricted to the same condition and graph group, and preserves cell-level parent-cluster provenance. Both Seurat metacell builders use a default gamma of 30 cells per metacell.
License: GPL-3
BugReports: https://github.com/GfellerLab/SuperCell/issues
